# List widget — 5 layout suggestions

Today the List widget renders a concept's instances two ways, auto-picked by tile
width: a dense `InstanceTable` (wide) or stacked `InstanceCard`s (narrow). The
`variant` field is `auto | cards`. The 5 below turn `variant` into a real menu of
presentations — each reads the same concept/fields/filter/order/limit/archived state,
only the row rendering changes.

Header chrome (🔒 quick-edit lock, ＋ create) is shared by all of them.

***

## 1. Table — spreadsheet

 Current wide mode. Sortable column headers, inline quick-edit cells, scalar fields only.
Best when the tile is wide and the user wants to scan/compare many fields at once.

```
┌ Vendors ───────────────────────────────── 🔒 ＋ ┐
│  Name          Status     Owner     MRR    Tier  │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│  Acme Corp     Active     K. Lee   $4.2k   ▲ A   │
│  Northwind     Trialing   J. Roy   $1.0k   ▽ B   │
│  Globex        Churned    —        $0      ▽ C   │
│  Initech       Active     M. Diaz  $8.7k   ▲ A   │
│  Hooli         Trialing   A. Chen  $3.3k   ▽ B   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Schema: none new (this is the existing `table`/wide path).

***

## 2. Cards — stack

Current narrow mode. First column is the title, next ≤3 fields become a meta line,
archived badge top-right. Best for a tall/skinny tile in a sidebar column.

```
┌ Vendors ───────────────────────── 🔒 ＋ ┐
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│ │ Acme Corp                  [Active] │  │
│ │ K. Lee · $4.2k · Tier A             │  │
│ └────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│ │ Northwind                [Trialing] │  │
│ │ J. Roy · $1.0k · Tier B             │  │
│ └────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│ │ Globex                    [Churned] │  │
│ │ — · $0 · Tier C                     │  │
│ └────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Schema: none new (existing `cards` path).

***

## 3. Line feed — compact rows

One borderless line per item: leading status dot, title, then a few right-aligned
field chips. Densest readable option — Linear's issue list. Great for "top N" tiles
where you want the most rows visible without a full grid.

```
┌ Vendors ──────────────────────────── 🔒 ＋ ┐
│  ● Acme Corp           K.Lee   $4.2k    2d  │
│  ◐ Northwind           J.Roy   $1.0k    5d  │
│  ○ Globex                —     $0       —   │
│  ● Initech            M.Diaz   $8.7k    1w  │
│  ◐ Hooli               A.Chen  $3.3k    3d  │
│  ● Umbrella            S.Park   $5.1k    4h  │
│  ○ Soylent               —     $0       —   │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   ▲ status dot maps to an enum field's color
```

Schema: `variant: "rows"`. Optional `statusField` to pick which enum drives the dot
(default: concept's first enum field). Reuses existing columns for the trailing chips.

***

## 4. Grouped — sectioned

Group rows under collapsible headers by an enum or relation field, each header showing
a count. Vertical cousin of the Kanban widget; good when one field is the primary axis
(status, owner, stage) but you still want a list, not a board.

```
┌ Vendors ─── group: Status ───────────── 🔒 ＋ ┐
│  ▼ Active · 2                                  │
│      Acme Corp        K.Lee      $4.2k         │
│      Initech          M.Diaz     $8.7k         │
│  ▼ Trialing · 2                                │
│      Northwind        J.Roy      $1.0k         │
│      Hooli            A.Chen     $3.3k         │
│  ▶ Churned · 3                                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   ▲ collapsed sections remember state per user
```

Schema: `variant: "grouped"` + required `groupBy: fieldId` (enum/relation/user).
Collapse state per-user-sticky, like quick-edit.

***

## 5. Gallery — tile grid

Cards reflowed into a responsive multi-column grid that fills tile width. Title +
status badge + 1–2 key fields per tile. Best for browsing many items at a glance in a
wide tile — people, accounts, anything you scan visually.

```
┌ Vendors ───────────────────────────── 🔒 ＋ ┐
│ ┌───────────┐ ┌───────────┐ ┌───────────┐    │
│ │ Acme Corp │ │ Northwind │ │ Globex    │    │
│ │ [Active]  │ │ [Trialing]│ │ [Churned] │    │
│ │ $4.2k · A │ │ $1.0k · B │ │ $0 · C    │    │
│ └───────────┘ └───────────┘ └───────────┘    │
│ ┌───────────┐ ┌───────────┐ ┌───────────┐    │
│ │ Initech   │ │ Hooli     │ │ Umbrella  │    │
│ │ [Active]  │ │ [Trialing]│ │ [Active]  │    │
│ │ $8.7k · A │ │ $3.3k · B │ │ $5.1k · A │    │
│ └───────────┘ └───────────┘ └───────────┘    │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   ▲ column count derived from measured widgetBox width
```

Schema: `variant: "gallery"`. Reuses InstanceCard rendering; column count from
`useWidgetBox()` width (same source `auto` already reads).

***

## Build forks

* `variant` enum: `auto | table | cards | rows | grouped | gallery` — keep `auto` as
  the width-driven default (table↔cards), the rest explicit. One contract field change.

* 3/4/5 are the net-new renderers; 1 & 2 already exist. Cheapest first ship: **rows (3)**
  — no new required config, pure renderer.

* Grouped (4) is the only one needing a new required-ish field (`groupBy`).

### Open questions

* Ship all 4 new variants or start with rows + gallery (no new required config)?

* Grouped: collapse state per-user-sticky (like quick-edit) or per-widget-config?

* Rows: status dot from explicit `statusField`, or auto-pick first enum?
